# Auth & RBAC

```typescript
enum PlatformRole {
  SUPER_ADMIN = 'SUPER_ADMIN',
  ADMIN = 'ADMIN',
  CUSTOMER = 'CUSTOMER',
  VENDOR = 'VENDOR',
  PROFESSIONAL = 'PROFESSIONAL',
}
```

## One identity per email

- One email = one lane: customer **or** store **or** professional **or** admin — never combine.
- Owners and staff share the same platform role (`VENDOR` / `PROFESSIONAL` / `ADMIN`).
- Ordinary platform staff use `ADMIN`; their ADMIN-scoped custom role defines responsibilities.
- Owner = has `VendorProfile` / `ProfessionalProfile` + system Owner membership (full access in own entity).
- Staff = same `platformRole`, **no** profile, one `TeamMember` + custom role.
- At most one non-deleted `TeamMember` per user, regardless of status.
- Customer APIs are `CUSTOMER`-only with ownership checks (no RBAC permissions).

## Login endpoints

- `POST /auth/login` — customer app (`CUSTOMER` only)
- `POST /auth/dashboard/login` — dashboard (`VENDOR`, `PROFESSIONAL`, `ADMIN`, `SUPER_ADMIN`)

## Guard chain

```
Throttler → JwtAuthGuard → RolesGuard → PermissionsGuard → ActiveContextGuard → OwnerOnlyGuard → OnboardingOnlyGuard
```

- `@Public()` — skip JWT
- `@Roles(PlatformRole.ADMIN)` — platform role; `SUPER_ADMIN` always passes
- `@Permissions('products:create')` — required for `/vendor|/admin` routes (default-deny). `/professional/` is planned and has no controllers yet.
- Coupon routes (`/admin/coupons`, `/vendor/coupons`) require `coupons:manage`.
- `@OwnerOnly()` — business owner only (or Super Admin)
- `@OnboardingOnly()` — owner onboarding routes (GET allowed after APPROVED; writes 400)
- `@RequireActiveContext(PermissionScope.VENDOR)` — matching server-derived context
- Owner system role = full access in own vendor/professional entity (not Platform Admin)
- `SUPER_ADMIN` = only unrestricted platform principal
- `@CurrentUser()` → `AuthenticatedUser`

## JWT (identity-only)

`{ userId, platformRole, impersonatedBy?, isImpersonation? }`

Never trust permissions or business context from the JWT.
`activeContext` is resolved server-side on every request from DB membership/owner state.

Vendor staff resolve store via `activeContext.entityId` (not `userId`).
Pre-approval vendors: onboarding-only until approved; Owner membership created on approval.

## Session (frontend)

Auth success (login / dashboard login / register / refresh / OTP verify) returns:

`{ accessToken, refreshToken, session }`

`GET /auth/session` returns the same `session` object (for app boot / hard refresh).

```typescript
session: {
  user: { id, name, email, platformRole },
  activeContext: { type, entityId, customRoleId, roleName, isOwner, isSuspended } | null,
  permissions: string[], // concrete keys; Owner = all scope keys; SUPER_ADMIN = all ADMIN keys
  flags: { needsOnboarding, isImpersonating, accessRevoked }
}
```

- No top-level `activeContext` on auth responses (use `session.activeContext`)
- No sidebar/menu from API — frontend maps `permissions` + flags to nav
- `needsOnboarding`: VENDOR/PROFESSIONAL with no context
- Impersonation start also returns `session` for the target (`flags.isImpersonating: true`)

## Context

- `GET /auth/contexts` — returns the single derived context (no switch)
- Context switching is disabled

## Impersonation

`POST /admin/impersonate/:userId` — Super Admin or elevated Admin (`users:impersonate`).
15m token, no refresh, cannot target platform staff, no nested impersonation.
Response includes target `session`. Audit start success/failure and every API call success/failure.

## Elevated permissions

Only in ADMIN scope. Only Super Admin may assign `isElevated` permissions.

## Invitations

- Vendor/professional staff: invite-only
- Platform staff: invite-only; ADMIN managers with `team:manage` may assign non-elevated roles whose permissions are a subset of their own
- Only Super Admin may assign elevated ADMIN roles
- ADMIN invitation input is `email` + `customRoleId`; the backend derives `platformRole=ADMIN`
- Call `GET /invitations/preview?token=` first — returns `nextAction` (CREATE_ACCOUNT | ACCEPT), `hasAccount`, `user {name,email}`, `sessionOnAccept`
- Single `POST /invitations/accept`: new users send name+password and receive tokens; existing users send invite token only (membership granted, no session unless caller JWT also matches)
- Invite token alone for an existing account grants membership but never mints a session (prevents passwordless takeover)
- Sending Bearer for the invited email alongside the invite token grants membership and re-issues tokens with the new activeContext
- Removed staff regain a free slot; an ex-admin can join vendor/professional after removal (lane switch applies atomically in the same accept transaction)
- After a successful accept, other PENDING invitations for the same email are revoked automatically
- Tokens hashed (SHA-256), single-use, expiring
- Expired invitations are immutable; create a replacement instead of resending
- One live pending invitation per normalized email and context

## OTP

6-digit numeric · 5 min expiry · max 3 failed attempts across recent OTP rows (15m window)
New OTP send cannot reset lockout.

## Bootstrap / seed

- Demo seed: requires `SEED_ALLOW_DEV_RESET=true`, blocked in production
- Password overwrite on seed only if `SEED_RESET_PASSWORDS=true`
- Production bootstrap: `pnpm bootstrap:super-admin` with `BOOTSTRAP_SUPER_ADMIN=true`
- Never reset existing SUPER_ADMIN password via bootstrap

## Security

Rate limit login, OTP send, OTP verify, register. Never log passwords or tokens.
`security` namespace platform settings (`cartMutationLimitPerMinute`, `checkoutLimitPerMinute`, `paymentVerifyLimitPerMinute`, `productBrowseLimitPerMinute`) are stored in the database but are not wired to `@Throttle`. Hardcoded decorator limits are authoritative.
`SUPER_ADMIN`, `ADMIN` cannot self-register.
Identical login failure messages (no account-status enumeration).
